I'm thrilled to hear that you'd like me to speak at a Xanadu Tech
Forum! There are quite a few things I'd like to talk about...  

What aspects of pie menus would the audience be most interested in?  I
could describe what they are, how they work, what they're good for,
their advantages over linear menus (the results of our experimental
comparison), and how they've been used in various applications.  I can
also talk about how to design easy to use pie menus (of interest to
people implementing application using pie menus), and how to roll your
own pie menus (of interest to people implementating or extending UI
toolkits).

I am presently writing up the work I've been doing on a visual
PostScript programming environment for NeWS... Graphical data
structure visualization and editing, programming and debugging by
direct manipulation, etc... This should make an interesting talk.
Inspired by smalltalk and the lisp machine, but my real goal is full
blown CyberSpace (to the extent that the technology and the user's
perception of reality can support it)!

